From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: a lost device's command lists are retired, and d3d9 says it is lost

A command list whose submission failed with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST - and every
one after it, which is not submitted at all - was dropped by the submission
thread rather than passed to the finish thread. Its destruction let go of
what it used, but its signals were never notified, and nobody woke a thread
already asleep in a resource wait (synchronizeUntil sleeps on the finish
thread's condition, which no lost command list ever reached): a Map that
began waiting on a resource before the failure slept for good, as no command
list finishes on a lost device. The finish thread already skips the wait for
a lost device; it now gets those command lists too, and notifies and wakes as
for any other. accel-virt's executor runs every guest Direct3D 11 session of
a GPU on one DXVK device, so one lost device must not leave any of them
waiting inside DXVK.

Direct3D 9 had no way to say its Vulkan device was lost: TestCooperativeLevel
now answers D3DERR_DEVICELOST once it is, which is what accel-virt's executor
asks of a host Direct3D 9 device that has no window.
---
diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
index 9b72bb2e..8213e308 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
@@ -223,6 +223,11 @@ namespace dxvk {
   HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE D3D9DeviceEx::TestCooperativeLevel() {
     D3D9DeviceLock lock = LockDevice();
 
+    // A Vulkan device that was lost is a device lost for good: an embedder
+    // drawing with no window asks here, as an application would.
+    if (unlikely(m_dxvkDevice->getDeviceStatus() == VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST))
+      return D3DERR_DEVICELOST;
+
     // Equivelant of D3D11/DXGI present tests. We can always present.
     if (likely(m_deviceLostState == D3D9DeviceLostState::Ok)) {
       return D3D_OK;
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_queue.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_queue.cpp
index e705ed91..0b598817 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_queue.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_queue.cpp
@@ -201,12 +201,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
       // On success, pass it on to the queue thread
       { std::unique_lock<dxvk::mutex> lock(m_mutex);
 
+        bool deviceLost = entry.result == VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST;
+
         bool doForward = (entry.result == VK_SUCCESS) ||
-          (entry.present.presenter != nullptr && entry.result != VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST);
+          (entry.present.presenter != nullptr && !deviceLost);
 
-        if (doForward) {
-          m_finishQueue.push(std::move(entry));
-        } else {
+        if (!doForward) {
           Logger::err(str::format("DxvkSubmissionQueue: Command submission failed: ", entry.result));
           m_lastError = entry.result;
 
@@ -214,6 +214,14 @@ namespace dxvk {
             m_device->waitForIdle();
         }
 
+        // A command list the device lost is retired all the same: the
+        // finish thread skips its wait, since the device is lost, and
+        // releases what it used and wakes whoever waits on it. Dropped
+        // here, its resources stayed in use for good, and a Map or a
+        // resource wait on any of them never returned.
+        if (doForward || (deviceLost && entry.submit.cmdList != nullptr))
+          m_finishQueue.push(std::move(entry));
+
         m_submitQueue.pop();
         m_submitCond.notify_all();
       }
